# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   H. Kang et al. (2025). FastTrack: a fast method to evaluate mass transport in solid leveraging universal machine learning interatomic potential.
#   AI for Science. doi:10.1088/3050-287x/ae0808  arXiv:2508.10505v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2508.10505v1 (sha256 4bed411be3b271cf...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 251 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kang2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the FastTrack workflow (grid sampling and interpolation of
# the potential energy surface of a migrating ion with a universal MLIP,
# with partial relaxation within 2.8 A) applied with pretrained GPTFF,
# CHGNet and MACE to twelve electrode and electrolyte materials, and GPTFF
# fine-tuned on PBE and PBE+U LiCoO2 data. All barriers and the
# fine-tuning test MAEs are given only in figures, so no error metric is
# encoded; the stated time per barrier is kept as a timing.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
